== a_line_without_y
error[Z0406]: `line` needs `y`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:3
  |
2 | m.line(year)
  |   ^^^^ `y` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `data.line(x, y, color: Var, by: Var | Vars)`

== a_line_of_a_variable_not_there
error[Z0101]: no variable `years` in `m`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:8
  |
2 | m.line(years, rate)
  |        ^^^^^ not a variable of m
  |
  = help: did you mean `year`? If you meant a category level, write it in quotes: `"year"`

== a_line_in_another_case
error[Z0102]: no variable `Rate` in `m`; names are case-sensitive
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:14
  |
2 | m.line(year, Rate)
  |              ^^^^ differs only in case from `rate`
  |
  = help: write `rate`

== a_line_coloured_by_a_number
error[Z0401]: `lines` draws each line in one colour, so `color` must show categories, but `rate` is a Float without value labels, which is shown on a continuous scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:3
  |
2 | m.line(year, rate, color: rate)
  |   ^^^^ a colour for each row, not for each line
  |
  = help: colour the lines by a variable of categories, as in `lines(color: union)`, or set one colour for this layer, as in `lines(color: "black")`

== a_line_coloured_by_a_string
error[Z0401]: `color` of `line` must be a Var, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:27
  |
2 | m.line(year, rate, color: "red")
  |                           ^^^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: name a variable of the frame, without quotes

== a_line_in_panels_by_a_variable_not_there
error[Z0101]: no variable `site` in `m`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:24
  |
2 | m.line(year, rate, by: site)
  |                        ^^^^ not a variable of m
  |
  = help: the variables of `m` are: year, rate, region, arm

== a_line_in_panels_by_one_variable_twice
note: 1 row with NA in year or rate dropped (line 2)
note: 1 break in a line where rate is NA (line 2)
note: 1 row with no neighbour to be joined to draws no line (line 2)
error[Z0401]: `by:` of `facet` names `region` twice
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:24
  |
2 | m.line(year, rate, by: [region, region])
  |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ one variable, twice
  |
  = help: a plot is parted by each variable once; leave the second out

== a_line_of_a_plot
error[Z0401]: `line` cannot be called on a Plot
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | m.plot(x: year).line(year, rate)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is a Plot
  |
  = help: `line` takes a Frame first; `x.line(...)` is `line(x, ...)`

